---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
import { CITY_LINE, SITE } from '../data/site';
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="How the IPJunction website collects and uses personal data.">
  <PageHead kicker="Legal" title="Privacy policy" lede="Last updated October 6, 2026. Draft pending legal review." />
  <section class="section container prose legal">
    <p>
      {SITE.legalName} ("IPJunction", "we") runs this website. This policy explains what personal data the site collects,
      why, and what choices you have. It covers this website only, not client engagements, which are governed by their
      own agreements.
    </p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Messages you send us.</strong> If you use the contact form we receive your name, email address, company (if
        given), topic and message. The form is delivered by Web3Forms, which forwards it to our inbox.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Bookings.</strong> If you open the scheduler, it loads from Cal.com, which processes the details you enter
        to book a call and may set its own cookies. It does not load unless you open it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Analytics, only with consent.</strong> If you accept analytics we use Umami to count page views. Umami sets
        no cookies and does not store IP addresses or build profiles. If you decline, no analytics script loads.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Hosting logs.</strong> The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub may log technical data such as IP
        addresses for security and operations under its own privacy statement.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What we store on your device</h2>
    <p>
      One item in your browser's local storage records your analytics choice so we do not ask again. You can change it
      at any time with "Cookie settings" in the footer, or clear it in your browser.
    </p>

    <h2>How we use your data</h2>
    <p>
      We use messages and bookings only to reply to you and to discuss potential work. We do not sell personal data or
      use it for advertising.
    </p>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>
      We keep correspondence for as long as needed to respond and for our ordinary business records, then delete it.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, delete or restrict use of your personal data.
      To exercise them, email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      {SITE.legalName}, {SITE.address.street}, {CITY_LINE}, USA.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
